boswas-bootsplash (1.0~alpha3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the Boswas OS boot, disk-unlock and shutdown screen
    (boswas-bootsplashd, boswas-bootsplash), written in Rust. It replaces
    the Plymouth theme of boswas-branding and Plymouth itself.
  * Damage-tracked software rendering on DRM/KMS dumb buffers, with a
    legacy frame buffer fallback; artwork, glyphs and colours (Boswas UI
    tokens) embedded at build time.
  * Passphrase prompt for encrypted disks: started in the initramfs,
    called by /lib/cryptsetup/askpass through a Plymouth-compatible client
    that exists only inside the initramfs; a systemd password agent for
    later requests; the text console as the fallback in every failure case.
  * The daemon drops privileges once running (no_new_privs, Landlock,
    capabilities) and a supervisor restores the console if it dies.

 -- Boswas OS Platform Team <os-platform@boswas.invalid>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
